In article <TJW.94Jun8163304@mthpgc.att.com> tjw@mthpgc.ATT.COM (Tom Wu) writes:

>I've had cases where I randomly polymorph out of the blue.  It's not a trap
>because I can step back on the square and have nothing happen.  I'm not
>wearing a ring of polymorph, either.  Why does this happen and how can I
>prevent it?

Polymorph traps vanish after you step on them. This is for game balance -
if it wasn't for this, there'd be nothing to stop you stepping on one again
and again until you turned into a vampire lord or something.

(they _don't_ vanish after a monster steps on them - bastards!)

So, you can never say with certainty "I didn't step on a polymorph" trap!
Unless you'd already walked over the square in question, and nothing had
happened, I guess. If you randomly polymorph out of the blue, you stepped
on a trap. If you're wearing dragonscale at the time, you'll polymorph
into the appropriate dragon.

How do you AVOID polymorph traps? Magic resistance..

